      "side": 1,
      "message": "My bad, sorry. IMO the DAWN_ASSERT only needs to check the *requested* swizzle \u003d\u003d RGBA, it\u0027s more complicated and unnecessary to check the metal-specific swizzle with R001 applied. The goal is just to have an ASSERT that validation has prevented us from reaching a case where we ignore the swizzle provided by the user.\n\nHow about factoring it out (I should have suggested that before):\n\n```\nstatic constexpr wgpu::TextureComponentSwizzle kR001Swizzle \u003d {\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::R,\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::Zero,\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::Zero,\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::One,\n};\nstatic constexpr wgpu::TextureComponentSwizzle kRGBASwizzle \u003d {\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::R,\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::G,\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::B,\n  wgpu::ComponentSwizzle::A,\n};\n\nstd::optional\u003cMTLTextureSwizzleChannels\u003e TextureView::ComputeMetalSwizzle() {\n  if (!SupportTextureComponentSwizzle(ToBackend(device)-\u003eGetMTLDevice())) {\n    // Validation should have prevented the user requesting a swizzle.\n    DAWN_ASSERT(AreSwizzleEquivalent(GetFrontendSwizzle(), kRGBASwizzle));\n    return {};\n  }\n\n  // If possible, a backend swizzle is always used for depth-stencil.\n  // If not, we returned {} above so G/B/A will be undefined.\n  if (texture-\u003eGetFormat().HasDepthOrStencil()) {\n    return ToMetalTextureSwizzleChannels(ComposeSwizzle(kR001Swizzle, GetFrontendSwizzle()));\n  }\n\n  if (!AreSwizzleEquivalent(GetFrontendSwizzle(), kRGBASwizzle)) {\n    return ToMetalTextureSwizzleChannels(GetFrontendSwizzle());\n  }\n\n  return {};\n}\n```\n\nThis will eliminate the need for several of the other helpers.",
